"""tdx-settings - settings panel for tdxd.

The window layout follows the 3DxWare 10 control panel (main window,
Advanced Settings, Buttons, LCD Manager, About), but everything it changes is
plain tdxd configuration: /etc/tdxd.conf and the per-application overlays in
/etc/tdxd.d/<name>.conf. Files are edited in place (comments are kept), then
the daemon is told to reload (`tdxctl reload`). Files that are not writable by
the user are written through `pkexec tdx-settings-helper`.

All artwork (device illustration, axis glyphs, key caps) is drawn here with
cairo; no 3Dconnexion images are used.
"""

